   "about" : "PrintBitMatrix goldens for the Image::PHash 0.3 printbitmatrix method. Each case drives the real installed Image::PHash 0.3 printbitmatrix through a fake $self carrying the fixed 32x32 row-major DCT fixture (DC 100.0 at index 0, AC coefficients ((i*13)%41)-20) shared with testdata/pipeline, testdata/mirror, and testdata/methods — NOT the Perl util.t Imager file-based M31.jpg pipeline; the captured output string is the golden. Cases cover NxN grid and bit-count geometry, reduce (filler positions), separator/filler options, the mirror/mirrorproof DCT variants, and the median/average_x extras. separator/filler record the raw option values (empty when unset), so the Go side must apply the Perl defaults: separator defaults to empty, filler defaults to a single space.",
